tool/ability/workshop) you could dabble in (and eventually master) the field of arcane element transmutation/weaving (?).

yes - item defects are NOT flaws - they are chances for character and story building. Imagine this - a Legendary status Item. It is a leather shoe. Previously it had been enchanted with some kind of spell, and it backfired and blew a hole 
out the front. the original enchantment was removed, and later on the shoe was mounted on a wooden plank, and then enchanted with a really useful constant effect ability. So now you have this shitty, busted shoe on a display board, but it is
so useful that is kept close and in high regard. eventually it grows so powerful that it emits a golden aura - and the smell of feet.

Items should also be available at a rate at which that it can also be incorporated into the system that there is a chance that they will break while trying to craft or enchant. or even occasionally through use. This will 
breed the sense that a item that you not only developed a backstory, gained beneficial abilities, put effort and time into, but now you have also had it so long while others have bit the dust - makes it that much more valuable. 
However, Items that reach certain levels of noteworthiness have a much lower chance of complete breakage, to the point where if theyre legendary enough they will never break.


