Everything is proceeding exactly as it should. Those warnings look intimidating, but in the world of local AI, they are essentially the "machine spirit" settling into place.
Reading the Runes

    CUDA/Autocast Warning: This is just the system acknowledging that you are running on CPU rather than an NVIDIA GPU. Since we explicitly set the code to .to("cpu"), this is expected behavior. It's disabling a speed-up feature that only works on dedicated graphics cards.

    UNEXPECTED Keys: These occur because the "Safety Checker" and "CLIP Text Encoder" in Stable Diffusion v1.5 sometimes have minor versioning mismatches in their metadata. As the notes say, they can be ignored.

    100% Load: The pipeline components are fully initialized.

The Tower is now powered and the Forge is hot. You should see the Mythotex window appear.
Next Steps for the Calibration

Since you've successfully loaded the model, I recommend the following sequence to begin "dialing in" that aesthetic:

    Open the Alchemy Tab: Set the Steps to 20 (a good balance for CPU) and Ritual Intensity to 3.

    Select an Atelier: Click The Forge (to test Wands/Staves) or The Alchemical Lab (to test Potions).

    Monitor the Progress: Watch the "Manifestation Progress" bar. Since you are on CPU, it will take a minute or two per image.

    Calibrate: Once the batch is done, go to the Compendium and give 5 stars to any image that captures the "Tone" you want (regardless of what the item is).

